<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/style.css">
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/index.css">
   <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
   <script>
      window.onload = () => {
         const successfulTransferText = document.getElementById("transferred-files");
         document.querySelectorAll("span#current-year").forEach(span => {
            span.textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
         });
         const server = new WebSocket(`ws://${location.host}`);
         server.onmessage = (event) => {
            const message = JSON.parse(event.data)
            successfulTransferText.textContent = message.value;
         }
      }
   </script>
   <title>Print from your phone online</title>
</head>
<body>
   <nav class="centered-content">
      <h1>Print From Web</h1>
   </nav>
   <main class="centered-content">
      <div id="introduction">
         <h2>Web based tool for file transfer + print:</h2>
         <hr>
         <p>Print from Web is a web based tool, through which you can transfer a document to another device and get the file opened in the receiver's browser, ready to print. This tool is very useful to you if your printer is not a network printer and you don't use any application for file sharing, and neither a compatible usb cable. Also useful if you want to send a document to someone else who can print it for you without them having to save it in their device.</p>
         <p>How did I get this idea? Well, I have all of the problems I just mentioned.</p>
         <p>Works well enough to transfer PDFs, another good thing is that the files aren't stored anywhere in the server side.</p>
         <h2>Get started:</h2>
         <hr>
         <p>
            <ul>
               <li>First, the sender needs to create a connection ID for the transfer first.</li>
               <li>Then, the receiver can join the connection with the ID.</li>
               <li>Once the receiver joins, the sender can select the file and send it.</li>
            </ul>
         </p>
      </div>
      <div id="options">
         <a href="/send"><button>Send</button></a>
         <a href="/receive"><button>Receive</button></a>
      </div>
      <div class="centered-content" style="flex-direction: column;">
         <p style="font-weight: 500;">Total files transferred online:</p>
         <p id="transferred-files-count"></p>
      </div>
   </main>
   <footer class="centered-content" style="grid-row: 3;">
      <div>
         <p>© <span id="current-year">2026</span> Soumyadeep Roy. All Rights Reserved.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
         <p>Check project: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/SoumyadeepRoy2006/print-from-web/tree/dev/">here</a></p>
      </div>
   </footer>
</body>
</html>